/ checkpointDetail holds detailed information about a checkpoint for display.\n    51→type checkpointDetail struct {\n    52→\tIndex            int\n    53→\tShortID          string\n    54→\tTimestamp        time.Time\n    55→\tIsTaskCheckpoint bool\n    56→\tMessage          string\n    57→\t// Interactions contains all prompt/response pairs in this checkpoint.\n    58→\t// Most strategies have one, but shadow condensations may have multiple.\n    59→\tInteractions []interaction\n    60→\t// Files is the aggregate list of all files modified (for backwards compat)\n    61→\tFiles []string\n    62→}\n    63→\n    64→func newExplainCmd() *cobra.Command {\n    65→\tvar sessionFlag string\n    66→\tvar commitFlag string\n    67→\tvar checkpointFlag string\n    68→\tvar noPagerFlag bool\n    69→\tvar shortFlag bool\n    70→\tvar fullFlag bool\n    71→\tvar rawTranscriptFlag bool\n    72→\tvar generateFlag bool\n    73→\tvar forceFlag bool\n    74→\tvar searchAllFlag bool\n    75→\n    76→\tcmd := &cobra.Command{\n    77→\t\tUse:   \"explain\",\n    78→\t\tShort: \"Explain a session, commit, or checkpoint\",\n    79→\t\tLong: `Explain provides human-readable context about sessions, commits, and checkpoints.\n    80→\n    81→Use this command to understand what happened during agent-driven development,\n    82→either for self-review or to understand a teammate's work.\n    83→\n    84→By default, shows checkpoints on the current branch. Use flags to explain a specific\n    85→session, commit, or checkpoint.\n    86→\n    87→Output verbosity levels (for --checkpoint):\n    88→  Default:         Detailed view with scoped prompts (ID, session, tokens, intent, prompts, files)\n    89→  --short:         Summary only (ID, session, timestamp, tokens, intent)\n    90→  --full:          Parsed full transcript (all prompts/responses from entire session)\n    91→  --raw-transcript: Raw transcript file (JSONL format)\n    92→\n    93→Summary generation (for --checkpoint):\n    94→  --