cli/checkpoint/committed.go`:\n\n```go\n// CheckpointAuthor contains author information for a checkpoint.\ntype CheckpointAuthor struct {\n\tName  string\n\tEmail string\n}\n\n// GetCheckpointAuthor retrieves the author of a checkpoint from the entire/sessions commit history.\n// Returns the author of the commit that contains this checkpoint's metadata.json file.\nfunc (s *GitStore) GetCheckpointAuthor(ctx context.Context, checkpointID id.CheckpointID) (CheckpointAuthor, error) {\n\t_ = ctx // Reserved for future use\n\n\trefName := plumbing.NewBranchReferenceName(paths.MetadataBranchName)\n\tref, err := s.repo.Reference(refName, true)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn CheckpointAuthor{}, nil // No sessions branch, no author\n\t}\n\n\t// Path to the checkpoint's metadata file\n\tmetadataPath := checkpointID.Path() + \"/\" + paths.MetadataFileName\n\n\t// Walk commit history looking for the commit that has this file\n\titer, err := s.repo.Log(&git.LogOptions{\n\t\tFrom:  ref.Hash(),\n\t\tOrder: git.LogOrderCommitterTime,\n\t})\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn CheckpointAuthor{}, nil\n\t}\n\tdefer iter.Close()\n\n\tvar author CheckpointAuthor\n\tvar foundCommit *object.Commit\n\n\terr = iter.ForEach(func(c *object.Commit) error {\n\t\ttree, treeErr := c.Tree()\n\t\tif treeErr != nil {\n\t\t\treturn nil\n\t\t}\n\n\t\t_, fileErr := tree.File(metadataPath)\n\t\tif fileErr != nil {\n\t\t\t// File doesn't exist in this commit - we've gone past the creation point\n\t\t\tif foundCommit != nil {\n\t\t\t\treturn errStopIteration\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\treturn nil\n\t\t}\n\n\t\t// File exists - track it (oldest one with file is the creator)\n\t\tfoundCommit = c\n\t\tauthor = CheckpointAuthor{\n\t\t\tName:  c.Author.Name,\n\t\t\tEmail: c.Author.Email,\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn nil\n\t})\n\n\treturn author, nil\n}\n```\n\nAdd `var errStopIteration = errors.New(\"stop iteration\")` if not already defined.\n\n**2. Update formatCheckpointOutput to accept and display author**\n\nIn `cmd/entire/cli/expla