\n\tfor _, c := range associatedCommits {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(&sb, \"  %s %s %s\\n\", c.ShortSHA, c.Date.Format(\"2006-01-02\"), c.Message)\n\t}\n} else {\n\tsb.WriteString(\"\\nCommits: No commits found on this branch\\n\")\n}\n```\n\n**3. Update runExplainCheckpoint to fetch and pass associated commits**\n\nAfter fetching the author, add:\n```go\nassociatedCommits, _ := getAssociatedCommits(repo, fullCheckpointID, searchAll)\n```\n\nUpdate the call to formatCheckpointOutput with the new signature.\n\nFor temporary checkpoints (explainTemporaryCheckpoint), pass nil for associatedCommits.\n\n**4. Update all test callers**\n\nAll existing tests call formatCheckpointOutput with `commitMessage string` - update them to pass `nil` or `[]associatedCommit{}` instead.\n\n**5. Add tests**\n\n- TestGetAssociatedCommits - test finding commits with matching trailer\n- TestFormatCheckpointOutput_WithAssociatedCommits - verify commits displayed\n- TestFormatCheckpointOutput_NoCommitsOnBranch - verify \"No commits found\" message\n\n## TDD approach\n1. Write test for getAssociatedCommits\n2. Implement getAssociatedCommits  \n3. Write test for associated commits display\n4. Update formatCheckpointOutput signature and implementation\n5. Update all callers\n6. Run full test suite\n7. Commit\n\n## Commands\n- `mise run test` - unit tests\n- `mise run lint` - lint check\n- `mise run fmt` - format code\n\nCommit message format:\n```\nfeat(explain): show associated commits in checkpoint detail view\n\nENT-212: Add getAssociatedCommits to find git commits that reference a\ncheckpoint ID via Entire-Checkpoint trailer. Display commits in checkpoint\ndetail view with SHA, date, and message. Respects --search-all flag and\nbranch filtering.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n```","agentId":"a704b03"},"toolUseID":"agent_msg_01V8Y9727g38iQ8fxrm6kA6y","parentToolUseID":"toolu_01JqEwB8V6a4ijUmF5UxcAUD","uuid":"1c982245-511e-4c71-b70a-f7087ac6a343","timestamp":"2026-02-04T04: